1
00:00:00,321 --> 00:00:06,821
This is ExportAgent, an AI export desk for apparel and textile exporters.

2
00:00:06,821 --> 00:00:13,821
A German buyer has just sent a revised purchase order: Rev 1 of PO NW-45120.

3
00:00:13,821 --> 00:00:20,321
Here is their email, with the purchase order attached as a PDF.

4
00:00:20,432 --> 00:00:27,432
Nemotron Nano extracted every field, with a confidence score and the exact source quote.

5
00:00:27,432 --> 00:00:34,432
Python then checks each one: is the quote really in the email, and do the sizes add up?

6
00:00:34,432 --> 00:00:40,932
The order keeps every version, and Python compares them field by field.

7
00:00:40,932 --> 00:00:46,432
The total is up 1,500 pieces, and the ex-factory date moved 15 days earlier.

8
00:00:46,432 --> 00:00:51,832
Navy alone is up 33%. Every change goes to the risk check.

9
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:57,833
Python found the new plan infeasible, so this run escalated to Nemotron Ultra.

10
00:00:57,833 --> 00:01:01,833
The factory is 4,186 pieces short of free capacity.

11
00:01:01,833 --> 00:01:05,700
The trace shows every step, and the Python result behind each flag.

12
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:10,700
Ultra chose to check Germany's import rules with a Tavily web search.

13
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:15,890
Its sources are kept as evidence. The labelling rule is listed under Info checked.

14
00:01:15,890 --> 00:01:21,890
Nemotron Super drafted the reply. A Python fact check verified all 14 values in it.

15
00:01:21,890 --> 00:01:28,290
Both delivery options, the full quantity on 8 December or a split shipment, were computed in Python.

16
00:01:28,313 --> 00:01:33,313
A person approves every reply. Nothing is emailed automatically.

17
00:01:33,315 --> 00:01:39,815
Capacity, lead times and invoice formats live in factory profiles.

18
00:01:39,815 --> 00:01:45,815
The same revision is infeasible in Tiruppur, but feasible in Dhaka, at 72% of free capacity.

19
00:01:45,815 --> 00:01:50,815
Switching profiles changes the exporter, the port and the paperwork.

20
00:01:50,848 --> 00:01:56,348
The buyer accepts the split shipment, so we record that decision.

21
00:01:56,348 --> 00:02:01,348
ExportAgent generates an invoice and a packing list for each shipment.

22
00:02:01,348 --> 00:02:06,948
Every number is computed in Python. Anything unknown prints as TO BE CONFIRMED.

23
00:02:06,977 --> 00:02:13,977
Every model call runs on Nebius Token Factory. Nano reads, Super drafts and judges risk.

24
00:02:13,977 --> 00:02:20,977
Ultra is used only when a trigger fires: about 21% of risk runs.

25
00:02:20,977 --> 00:02:27,977
Measured live, a whole email costs under one cent: $0.0094.

26
00:02:27,977 --> 00:02:35,377
On a held-out test set, it found every high-risk issue.

27
00:02:35,387 --> 00:02:43,987
ExportAgent: every buyer email read, checked and answered, with a person in control.
